* text eol=lf

# Binary files must never go through the line-ending normalization above: a JPEG or font file is
# arbitrary binary data that can coincidentally contain byte pairs that look like CRLF, and the
# `text` attribute forces git to "normalize" those on commit -- silently corrupting the file (this
# is exactly what happened to Pictures/wallpaper-chezmoi/artemis.jpg: the committed blob ended up
# 40 bytes smaller than the working-tree file, byte-for-byte identical apart from a handful of
# coincidental CRLF-look-alikes that don't actually mean anything in JPEG's binary format).
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
*.gif binary
*.bmp binary
*.ico binary
*.ttf binary
*.otf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.plist binary